Provenance caveat (from the paper and camel_morph's db_maker.py): the lexicon
was seeded from CALIMA-Star/SAMA and reworked by hand, and the lex_logprob and
pos_lex_logprob values are estimated from the Penn Arabic Treebank training
split. The noprob variant removes those values.

Changes in this variant (CC BY 4.0 section 3(a)(1)(B)): derived from the noprob
variant (no pos_logprob/lex_logprob/pos_lex_logprob values) and converted to
CrispEmbed's binary analyzer format (crispembed-camel-morph-bin-v1). Only these
features are kept: diac, lex, root, pos, prc3, prc2, prc1, prc1.5, prc0, per,
asp, vox, mod, form_gen, gen, form_num, num, stt, cas, enc0, enc1, enc2, rat,
source. bw is kept on the NOAN backoff stems only. All other features (gloss,
bw, caphi, pattern, pattern_abstract, cm_*, catib6, ud, the tokenization
features, correctness, mid_root_diac) were removed. Prefixes, suffixes, stems,
categories, compatibility tables, DEFAULT and STEMBACKOFF entries are otherwise
unchanged.
